Subject: plug-in: an uber shader's program found without an allocation, the vertex textures told when they change, the draws' switches

What -hakiosDrawOnce: did at every draw that is not the draw's own:

- -hakiosProgramFor: looked the deciding buffer's bytes up through an NSData made for the key, an NSDictionary and
  @synchronized: an allocation and an autorelease, a hash of the object and two trips through the runtime's lock
  table, for every draw of every pipeline with an uber shader -- CoreAnimation's are. The contents seen are now plain
  arrays in the pipeline (the bytes, their hash, the program; 64 as before) under an os_unfair_lock held for the
  search alone; the bytes are read once, onto the stack. The compilation on its queue fills its slot when it is done.
- hakios_metal_cb_set_vertex_textures was called before every draw. The vertex stage's textures and samplers are the
  command buffer's state until told otherwise: told at an encoder's first draw and after one of them changes.
- metal_keep=0 and metal_verify=1 (boot-args or /var/tmp/metal.args), read with the first queue:
  hakios_metal_draw_states. The first has every draw judged and written whole -- the stream is the same, so it is
  the A/B switch for what the kept states save, and a bisect's. The second checks every draw taken from a kept state
  against itself written whole and fails the command buffer at a difference, saying which words: a check to run once
  on the phone, at more than twice a draw's cost.

Built for iOS with clang 18.1.8 (build-bundle.sh); not run on a device from here.


